#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Amp orb setup. MyGitApp is a macOS SwiftUI app: it does not build on this Linux orb, which only edits code
# and runs git and gh (both preinstalled). Xcode, `swift build` and `swift test` run on the thread's Mac
# satellite, which resolves the SwiftPM dependencies itself. So nothing is installed here; setup only leaves
# notes for agents working in the orb.
set -euo pipefail

notes="$HOME/.config/amp/AGENTS.md"
begin="<!-- mygitapp orb notes: begin -->"
end="<!-- mygitapp orb notes: end -->"

echo "Writing MyGitApp notes to $notes"
mkdir -p "$(dirname "$notes")"
touch "$notes"
# A stale snapshot already has the block: replace it rather than append a second one.
sed -i "/^$begin\$/,/^$end\$/d" "$notes"
cat >> "$notes" <<EOF
$begin
# MyGitApp in an orb

- This orb has no Swift toolchain: MyGitApp only builds on macOS. Start a Mac satellite (the default image works)
  and run \`swift build\`, \`swift test\` and \`scripts/bundle.sh debug\` there with mac_shell. A cold build,
  SwiftPM dependencies included, takes about 15 s.
- Screen checks use the README's \`MYGITAPP_OPEN\` / \`MYGITAPP_TAB\` / \`MYGITAPP_SNAPSHOT\` hooks.
  \`MYGITAPP_DELAY\` (seconds, default 6) delays the capture: a long delay keeps the app open so you can drive it
  with \`cliclick\` (\`brew install cliclick\`) and capture it with \`screencapture -x\`. Text typed with cliclick
  stops SwiftUI hover updates in the whole window until relaunch, so check hover states before typing.
- The app takes its GitHub token from \`gh auth token\`. gh on the Mac is logged out and its keychain is locked
  (\`security add-generic-password\` fails), so log gh in without printing the token: on the orb, write
  \`gh auth token\` to a 0600 file outside the repo and serve it from 127.0.0.1 with \`python3 -m http.server\`;
  forward that port with mac_sidecar start \`forward_ports\`; once the file is written, run on the Mac
  \`curl -s http://127.0.0.1:PORT/FILE > /tmp/t && gh auth login --with-token < /tmp/t; rm -f /tmp/t\`.
  Then stop the server, delete the file, and run \`gh auth logout\` on the Mac when done. This token reads public
  repos; the sidebar's "HTTP 403 : Resource not accessible by integration" (notifications) is expected.
- slaynn/mygitapp often has no open PR. Open PRs of public repos, such as gonzalezreal/swift-markdown-ui,
  render fine for checking the PR screens.
$end
EOF
echo "Done"
